ution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307142} :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{t}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305195} :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308340}] :question/math-academy-id "q-333134" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{2}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306262} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answe